              1. The Science of Dog Years to Human Years Conversion
            </h3>
            <p>
              The popular rule that "1 dog year equals 7 human years" is a myth. According to the American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA), dogs age much faster during their first two years of life, after which aging rates depend heavily on <strong>breed size</strong> (Small, Medium, Large, Giant).
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--ink-primary)] tracking-tight">
              2. Breed Size Aging & Sleep Requirements
            </h3>
            <p>
              Larger dogs reach senior status much earlier than smaller dogs. Puppies require 18–20 hours of sleep per day, adult dogs need 12–14 hours, and senior dogs require 14–18 hours of dedicated rest.
            </p>
          </section>
        </>
      )}

      {page === 'baby' && (
        <>
          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--ink-primary)] tracking-tight">
              1. Pediatric Milestone Tracking in Weeks & Months
            </h3>
            <p>
              During an infant's first year, measuring age in completed weeks and months is crucial for tracking growth charts, vaccination timelines, and motor skill development.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--ink-primary)] tracking-tight">
              2. Premature Birth Gestational Corrected Age Formula
            </h3>
            <p>
              For babies born prematurely (before 37 weeks of gestation), pediatricians use <strong>corrected age</strong>. If a 16-week-old baby was born 4 weeks early, their corrected age is 12 weeks. Motor milestones should be evaluated based on corrected age until 2 years of age.
            </p>
          </section>
        </>
      )}

      {page === 'datediff' && (
        <>
          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--ink-primary)] tracking-tight">
              1. Calculating Date Differences & Time Intervals
            </h3>
            <p>
              Whether computing age gaps between family members, event countdowns, or project duration intervals, our Date Difference Calculator accounts for month lengths, leap year days, and exact time of day.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section class="space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[var(--ink-primary)] tracking-tight">
              2. How Old Was My Parent When I Was Born?
            </h3>
            <p>
              To calculate your mother's or father's age when you were born, set their Date of Birth as Date 1 and your Date of Birth as Date 2. The tool computes their exact age in years, months, and days on your birthday.
            </p>
          </section>
        </>
      )}

    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- Route-Specific Extra Blocks -->
